# TextFSM template: Nokia SR OS / TiMOS `show router … bgp summary`.
#
# Sample output (truncated, fixed-width classic-CLI table):
#   ===============================================================================
#   BGP Summary
#   ===============================================================================
#   Legend : D - Dynamic Neighbor
#   ===============================================================================
#   Neighbor
#   Description
#                  AS PktRcvd InQ  Up/Down   State|Rcv/Act/Sent (Addr Family)
#                     PktSent OutQ
#   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   10.0.0.2
#                65001    1234   0 1d02h00m  500/450/600 (IPv4)
#                         1235   0
#   10.0.0.3
#                65002       0   0 00h00m00s Active
#                            0   0
#   2001:db8::2
#                65003     234   0 00h01m00s 100/95/200 (IPv6)
#                          235   0
#
# Peer rows span three physical lines: peer-IP, AS+counters, and a
# trailing counters-only line. The middle line carries the State
# column (or Rcv/Act/Sent triplet on Established peers). The
# (IPv4)/(IPv6) suffix names the address family.
Value Filldown local_asn (\d+)
Value Filldown router_id ([0-9a-fA-F:.]+)
Value Required peer_ip ([0-9a-fA-F:.]+)
Value peer_asn (\d+)
Value uptime (\S+)
Value state (\S+)
Value prefixes_received (\d+)
Value prefixes_accepted (\d+)
Value prefixes_sent (\d+)
Value address_family (\S+)

Start
  ^BGP\s+Summary
  ^Neighbor\s*$$ -> Peers
  ^-+\s*$$ -> Peers

Peers
  # Peer-IP-only line (first physical line of a row).
  ^${peer_ip}\s*$$
  # Established session: middle line carries AS, counters, uptime and
  # the Rcv/Act/Sent triplet plus address-family label.
  ^\s+${peer_asn}\s+\d+\s+\d+\s+${uptime}\s+${prefixes_received}/${prefixes_accepted}/${prefixes_sent}\s+\(${address_family}\)\s*$$ -> Record
  # Non-Established session: middle line carries AS, counters, uptime
  # and a single state keyword.
  ^\s+${peer_asn}\s+\d+\s+\d+\s+${uptime}\s+${state}\s*$$ -> Record
  # Trailing counters-only line — skipped.
  ^\s+\d+\s+\d+\s*$$
  ^-+\s*$$
  ^\s*$$ -> Start
